  "about": "I’m a Software Engineer focused on building high-performance software that solves complex engineering problems. Most recently, I’ve been developing software for the motorsport industry, creating tools that help engineers analyze telemetry, simulate vehicle performance, and optimize race car setup.\n\nI specialize in C#, .NET, Java, Spring, TypeScript, React, and Electron, with a passion for designing scalable architectures, improving system performance, and delivering intuitive user experiences. I enjoy working on systems that process large amounts of data, streamline complex workflows, and enable engineers to make better decisions.\n\nMy interests extend beyond writing code. I’m passionate about software architecture, distributed systems, local-first software, developer experience, and building products that are both technically elegant and practical. I enjoy collaborating with cross-functional teams, mentoring engineers, and continuously learning new technologies and approaches to software development.\n\nI’m always interested in connecting with people who are passionate about software engineering, emerging technologies, and solving challenging problems.",
